    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Educational reform should be guided by research to make policies that can resolve issues facing the education system in Pakistan today. This was concluded by Professor Anwar Ahmed Zai, Chairman, Board of Intermediate Education, Karachi, at a policy dialogue on Educational Policy Reform, held at Aga Khan University's Institute for Educational Development (AKU-IED). \" Education in developing countries needs repositioning, envisioning, and reshaping to address the challenges of globalisation, a growing knowledge society and knowledge-based economy,\" said Professor Zai.",
